hich the model has no basis to size.","kind":"energy","tolerance_pct":20,"pass":false}],"assumptions":["Working solution productivity 10 g H2O2 per litre (assumed, typical for EAQ solutions); it sets pump and vessel sizes, not the mass balance.","2% of the hydrogen is vented with the hydrogenator purge and 3% of the reacted hydrogen ends as water (over hydrogenation, peroxide decomposition); both assumed to land inside the BREF hydrogen range.","Reaction heat is the overall H2 + O2 -> H2O2 enthalpy, split evenly between the hydrogenation and oxidation coolers for sizing (assumed split).","Spent air leaves the condenser saturated at 40 C; solvent losses and the carbon adsorber are not in the mass balance.","Quinone make up 1.0 kg/t (BREF 0.5 to 2.5) leaves as degraded quinone for incineration at 500 USD/t.","0.2% of the peroxide is lost with the column overhead water.","Product sold as 50% solution; the price is per tonne of 50% solution, so 100% H2O2 is valued at twice it.","Vacuum column reboiler driven by mechanical vapour recompression of its own overhead (10 K condensing approach, 10% steam trim)."],"notes":[]}